       [--log-level trace|debug|info|warning|error|critical|off]
       serves OpenAI Responses/Chat Completions and Anthropic Messages endpoints
       --default-max-tokens fixes the output budget of requests that omit a limit; unset, such a request gets the largest budget that still lets every lane be admitted at once (the remaining context with one lane)
       --max-request-mib defaults to 384 and is enforced before JSON parsing
       --media-cache-mib defaults to 1024; 0 disables retained media reuse
       --media-live-mib defaults to 2048 and bounds all live BF16 patch payloads
       --media-preprocess-threads defaults to 0 (auto, at most 16 workers)
       --request-log-jsonl appends full-precision server/request records
       --model-id overrides the artifact metadata.name reported by the server
       Responses state is process-local and bounded to 1024 records / 256 MiB by default
       --log-stats-interval-ms defaults to 5000; 0 disables periodic throughput logs
       --vision enables media and loads the fixed Vision GPU allocations
       --vision-residency overlay keeps the Vision tower in host memory and borrows device memory per image
       --vision-max-merged bounds the merged tokens of one media item (default 16384); larger media is downscaled
       --kv-capacity auto leaves 1024 MiB of sizing headroom
       --max-prefill-lanes N (default 1, at most --max-concurrency) lets that many requests prefill at once: each prefill unit goes to the lane with the shortest remaining prompt suffix, so a short or prefix-cached prompt is not stuck behind a very long one; the KV capacity must hold the long prompt and the short ones together. A lane passed over --prefill-max-skip units (default 8) is served before any shorter one
       --decode-rounds-per-prefill N runs that many decode rounds after each prefill unit while other requests are generating (default 0 = --prefill-chunk / 64, so 16 at the default chunk of 1024); 1 alternates strictly, which leaves a decoding stream a few tokens per second while a long prompt prefills; a larger N keeps streams responsive and makes the prefill finish later
       --prefill-cublas hands wide prefill GEMMs to cuBLAS: a large prefill speedup for a small perplexity cost (docs/performance.md), off by default, and it wants a larger --prefill-chunk to pay; --no-prefill-cublas-projections keeps the attention and GDN input projections off that route
       --lookup-ngram N adds context-lookup drafting alongside --spec: the last N tokens are matched against the sequence so far and what followed is proposed; it is exact, and 0 (the default) disables it
       --no-prefix-reuse disables compatible-prefix caching (enabled by default)
       --auto-prefix-grid offers shared candidates on a token grid so unrelated callers whose prompts start alike share a cached prefix without any client hint; a grid frontier is only published once two callers have both asked for it
       --auto-long-anchors N proposes a private long anchor at each of the last N message boundaries of every prompt, so a client that rewrites recent history restores at the anchor below the edit instead of re-prefilling from zero; it defaults to and is clamped to --max-long-anchors-per-continuation (raise that and --host-state-slots for deeper edits); 0 disables
       --progress-anchor-tokens N proposes a private long anchor at every multiple of N tokens of a prompt (default 16384, minimum 256) and keeps the anchors a cancelled prefill already holds, so a client that times out on a very long prompt and retries resumes from the last anchor instead of prefilling from zero; it shares the --max-long-anchors-per-continuation budget with --auto-long-anchors; 0 disables
       --slot-save-path DIR enables POST /slots/{id}?action=save|restore|erase, which writes a retained session to a file in DIR or restores one from it
       --auto-save-evicted writes a retained session back to the slot file it was last saved to or restored from before an involuntary eviction destroys it (requires --slot-save-path; erase never saves)
       --no-exit-on-engine-failure keeps the process alive when the Engine latches unavailable after repeated worker failures; by default it logs FATAL and exits with status 3 after a short grace period so a supervisor can restart it
       context cache defaults: device-state=max-concurrency, private=2x concurrency, shared=max(max-concurrency,4), anchors=2; Host state=8 slots, Host KV=8192 MiB
       --device-state-slots is extra checkpoint capacity beyond active lanes; --host-kv-mib uses MiB
       --auto-host-cache sizes Host state slots, Host KV and both catalogs from the host memory free after the model loads (all but --host-cache-reserve-mib, default 3072, an eighth of it for state slots); it replaces the four explicit Host capacity options
       --host-cache-max-mib N caps what --auto-host-cache pins, for machines whose memory other tenants share (default: no cap)
       --host-cache-percent N caps it at N% (1-100) of the machine's total memory (or its container's limit) whatever is free at startup; the smallest of this, the cap and the free memory less the reserve applies. With vision on, the reserve also covers --media-cache-mib and --media-live-mib
       --default-thinking-budget caps model-origin thinking for enabled requests; control tokens count toward the request output limit
       --preserve-thinking retains closed-turn assistant reasoning in later prompts
       --graft NAME=PATH loads a phantom-kv prefill graft (a safetensors container with a .json sidecar beside it); a request selecting it with "graft": "NAME" runs as if the graft's hidden turn preceded its own messages. Repeatable
       --default-graft NAME applies a loaded graft to every request that states none; a request opts out with "graft": ""
       --reasoning-effort is the effort of thinking-enabled requests that state none; request values override it; like request values, minimal runs as low and high/max as xhigh
       sampler defaults come from the loaded model and resolved thinking mode; server flags and request fields override individual values.
       --greedy forces temperature 0 (exact argmax).
       --version prints the build version and exits.
